I now have everything. Here is the complete map of the repository.

---

# Overview

Key finding: an **"invoices" feature already exists end-to-end** (frontend `features/invoices/`, backend `Invoice*.java`, migrations V4–V6, REST YAMLs). The current invoice model is `UNPAID`/`PAID` with a `pay` action. However, `e2e/specs/acceptance.spec.ts` describes a **not-yet-implemented target**: a `DRAFT → SENT → PAID` lifecycle with an `invoice-send-<id>` action and an `INVOICE_SENT id=.. amount=..` audit record. So the "invoices feature to add" is most likely evolving the existing one to that lifecycle. I cover both the existing invoices code and the projects/clients templates so you can model either way.

Conventions are documented authoritatively in `/home/daniel/ui-sandbox/CLAUDE.md` (5 frontend rules + backend layout). Note `ui/` contains only `money.ts` — there are **no shared button/table/panel primitives**; tables/buttons/forms are written inline per feature with `data-testid`s. `data-testid` is immutable public API.

---

# 1. Front-end (`src/main/frontend`)

## File trees

`routes/`:
```
routes/__root.tsx
routes/index.tsx
routes/dashboard.tsx
routes/clients.tsx              (layout: <Outlet/>)
routes/clients.index.tsx        (list)
routes/clients.$clientId.tsx    (detail)
routes/projects.tsx             (layout: <Outlet/>)
routes/projects.index.tsx       (list)
routes/projects.$projectId.tsx  (detail)
```
(No invoices route — invoices render inside `projects.$projectId.tsx`.)

`features/`:
```
features/home/nav.slot.tsx
features/dashboard/{nav.slot.tsx, queries.ts, DashboardSummary.tsx}
features/clients/{nav.slot.tsx, open.slot.tsx, search.slot.tsx, queries.ts,
                  ClientForm.tsx, ClientsTable.tsx, ClientProjectsTable.tsx}
features/projects/{nav.slot.tsx, open.slot.tsx, queries.ts, ProjectForm.tsx, ProjectsTable.tsx}
features/invoices/{queries.ts, InvoiceForm.tsx, InvoicesTable.tsx,
                   status.slot.tsx, pay.slot.tsx, sort.slot.tsx, due.slot.tsx, issued.slot.tsx}
```

`slots/`:
```
slots/Slot.tsx        (defineSlot mechanism — do not edit)
slots/registry.ts     (store — do not edit)
slots/discover.ts     (import.meta.glob of features/**/*.slot.tsx — do not edit)
slots/defs/appNav.ts
slots/defs/clientRow.ts        id 'client.row'    ctx {clientId}
slots/defs/clientsToolbar.ts   id 'clients.toolbar'
slots/defs/projectRow.ts       id 'project.row'   ctx {projectId}
slots/defs/invoiceRow.ts       id 'invoice.row'   ctx {invoiceId, projectId, status}
slots/defs/invoicesToolbar.ts  id 'invoices.toolbar' ctx {projectId}
```

`ui/` = `.gitkeep` + `money.ts` only. `api/` = `http.ts` only. `url/` = `useSearchParam.ts` only. `query/` = `queryClient.ts` only.

## The slot mechanism — `slots/Slot.tsx`
`defineSlot<Ctx>(id)` returns `{ id, Slot, fill }`. `Slot` renders a `Fragment` (never a wrapper div, so it works inside `<thead>/<tr>`) mapping `forSlot(id)` sorted by `order` then file path. A feature file exports `contribution = SomeSlot.fill({ order, Component })`. `slots/discover.ts` glob-imports every `features/**/*.slot.tsx` eagerly for side-effect registration. `slots/registry.ts` is a plain array store; `forSlot` filters by `slot` id and sorts `a.order - b.order || a.from.localeCompare(b.from)`.

Example slot def (`slots/defs/invoiceRow.ts`):
```ts
import { defineSlot } from '../Slot';
export const InvoiceRow = defineSlot<{ invoiceId: number; projectId: number; status: string }>(
  'invoice.row',
);
```
`slots/defs/appNav.ts`: `export const AppNav = defineSlot('app.nav');`

## Infra files (do not edit)

`api/http.ts`: `send<T>` throws on non-2xx, returns `undefined` for 204 else parsed JSON. Exports `getJson<T>(path)` and `postJson<T>(path, body)` (sets `Content-Type: application/json`, `JSON.stringify`).

`query/queryClient.ts`:
```ts
import { QueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query';
export const queryClient = new QueryClient({
  defaultOptions: {
    queries: { retry: false, refetchOnWindowFocus: false },
    mutations: { retry: false },
  },
});
```

`url/useSearchParam.ts`: `useSearchParam<T>(key, decode)` returns `[value, set]`; `set(undefined|'' )` deletes the key, `navigate({ to: '.', search: prev => ..., replace: true })`. Decoders exported: `asString`, `asNumber`, `asFlag`.

`ui/money.ts`: `formatMoney(amount) => \`$${Number(amount).toFixed(2)}\``.

`routes/__root.tsx`: `createRootRouteWithContext<{queryClient}>()` with `validateSearch: (search) => search` (open namespace); renders `<nav data-testid="app-nav"><AppNav.Slot/></nav>` and `<main data-testid="app-home"><Outlet/></main>` inside `<div data-testid="app-root">`.

## Nav slot example (`features/projects/nav.slot.tsx`)
```tsx
import { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router';
import { AppNav } from '../../slots/defs/appNav';
export const contribution = AppNav.fill({
  order: 20,
  Component: () => (
    <Link to="/projects" data-testid="nav-projects">Projects</Link>
  ),
});
```
Nav orders in use: home 0, dashboard 5, clients 10, projects 20. An invoices nav (if it gets a top-level page) would pick an unused order.

## List route pattern (`routes/projects.index.tsx`)
`createFileRoute('/projects/')` → component renders `<section data-testid="projects-page"><ProjectForm/><ProjectsTable/></section>`. Clients list additionally renders `<ClientsToolbar.Slot/>` between form and table.

`ProjectsTable.tsx`: `useQuery({ queryKey: projectsKey, queryFn: fetchProjects })`; returns `null` while no data; `<p data-testid="projects-empty">` when empty; else `<table data-testid="projects-table">` with `<tr data-testid={\`project-row-${id}\`}>`, cells `data-testid="project-name"`, `"project-client"`, and a trailing `<td><ProjectRow.Slot projectId={id}/></td>`.

`ProjectForm.tsx`: `useState` only for the in-flight fields (`name`, `clientId`); `useQuery(clientsKey, fetchClientOptions)` for the `<select data-testid="project-form-client">`; `useMutation({ mutationFn: createProject, onSuccess: () => invalidateQueries({queryKey: projectsKey}) })`. testids: `project-form`, `project-form-name`, `project-form-client`, `project-form-submit`.

## Detail route pattern (`routes/projects.$projectId.tsx`)
```tsx
import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router';
import { InvoiceForm } from '../features/invoices/InvoiceForm';
import { InvoicesTable } from '../features/invoices/InvoicesTable';
export const Route = createFileRoute('/projects/$projectId')({ component: ProjectDetailPage });
function ProjectDetailPage() {
  const { projectId } = Route.useParams();
  const id = Number(projectId);
  return (
    <section data-testid="project-detail">
      <InvoiceForm projectId={id} />
      <InvoicesTable projectId={id} />
    </section>
  );
}
```
Layout route `routes/projects.tsx`: `createFileRoute('/projects')({ component: () => <Outlet /> })`. Clients mirror this exactly (`clients.$clientId.tsx` renders `<section data-testid="client-detail"><ClientProjectsTable clientId={id}/></section>`).

The "open" row action (`features/projects/open.slot.tsx`) fills `ProjectRow` at order 0 with a `<Link to="/projects/$projectId" params={{projectId:String(projectId)}} data-testid={\`project-open-${projectId}\`}>Open</Link>`. Clients' `open.slot.tsx` is identical for `client-open-<id>`.

## Existing invoices feature (the closest model / likely target of the change)

`features/invoices/queries.ts`:
```ts
import { getJson, postJson } from '../../api/http';
export type Invoice = {
  id: number; projectId: number; amount: number;
  status: string; issuedDate: string; dueDate: string;
};
export const invoicesKey = (projectId: number) => ['invoices', projectId] as const;
export const INVOICE_SORT_PARAM = 'invoiceSort';
export function fetchInvoices(projectId: number): Promise<Invoice[]> {
  return getJson<Invoice[]>(`/api/invoices/${projectId}`);
}
export function createInvoice(input: { projectId: number; amount: number }): Promise<Invoice> {
  return postJson<Invoice>('/api/invoices', input);
}
export function payInvoice(invoiceId: number): Promise<Invoice> {
  return postJson<Invoice>(`/api/invoices/${invoiceId}/pay`, {});
}
```

`InvoicesTable.tsx`: queries `invoicesKey(projectId)`; reads `INVOICE_SORT_PARAM` via `useSearchParam`; if `sort==='due'` sorts a copy by `dueDate.localeCompare`; computes `total` by reducing amounts. Renders `<InvoicesToolbar.Slot projectId={projectId}/>`, then `<table data-testid="project-invoices-table">` with rows `data-testid={\`invoice-row-${id}\`}`, cell `data-testid="invoice-amount"` (formatMoney), then `<InvoiceRow.Slot invoiceId projectId status/>`, and a trailing `<p data-testid="project-invoices-total">`.

`InvoiceForm.tsx`: `useState` amount+error; validates `>0`; `useMutation(createInvoice, onSuccess → invalidate invoicesKey(projectId))`. testids `invoice-form`, `invoice-form-amount`, `invoice-form-submit`, `invoice-form-amount-error`.

Invoice row slots (all fill `InvoiceRow`, each its own file, ordered):
- `issued.slot.tsx` order 4 → `<td data-testid="invoice-issued">` (re-queries invoicesKey, finds own row).
- `due.slot.tsx` order 5 → `<td data-testid="invoice-due">`.
- `status.slot.tsx` order 10 → `<td data-testid="invoice-status">{status}</td>` (reads status from ctx).
- `pay.slot.tsx` order 20 → `<td><button data-testid={\`invoice-pay-${invoiceId}\`}>` with `useMutation(() => payInvoice(invoiceId), onSuccess → invalidate invoicesKey(projectId))`.

`sort.slot.tsx` fills `InvoicesToolbar` order 10 → `<button data-testid="invoice-sort-due" aria-pressed={sort==='due'} onClick={() => setSort('due')}>` owning `INVOICE_SORT_PARAM`.

Note the pattern for a **new per-row action / status transition** (e.g. an `invoice-send-<id>` button and a `DRAFT/SENT/PAID` status): it is a new `features/invoices/send.slot.tsx` filling `InvoiceRow`, plus a new POST endpoint + logic class + a Flyway migration if the status set/default changes — no edits to existing files. The `pay.slot.tsx` is the exact template for such an action; `status` is already in the slot ctx so a Component can conditionally render (e.g. show pay only when `status==='SENT'`).

`features/clients/queries.ts` also shows client-side validation shared with the server: `EMAIL_PATTERN = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/`, `isValidEmail`, `matchesClientSearch`, plus `clientProjectsKey = (id) => ['clients', id, 'projects']`.

---

# 2. Back-end

## REST endpoint tree (`src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/`)
```
clients.GET.yml                       -> ClientsGet
clients.POST.yml                      -> ClientsPost
clients/{clientId}/projects.GET.yml   -> ClientProjectsGet
projects.GET.yml                      -> ProjectsGet
projects.POST.yml                     -> ProjectsPost
invoices/{projectId}.GET.yml          -> InvoicesGet
invoices.POST.yml                     -> InvoicesPost
invoices/{id}/pay.POST.yml            -> InvoicePay
dashboard/summary.GET.yml             -> DashboardSummaryGet
```
Every YAML is just a comment + `service:\n  class: net.officefloor.hq.app.<Logic>`. Path = file path under `api/`; method = filename segment; `{param}` = path param. Must live under `api/` (SpaConfig only bypasses SPA for `api/`).

Example (`invoices/{id}/pay.POST.yml`):
```yaml
# POST /api/invoices/{id}/pay -> mark an invoice paid, recording an audit entry (InvoicePay.service).
service:
  class: net.officefloor.hq.app.InvoicePay
```

## Logic class conventions
A logic class is a plain class with a `service(...)` method. Injected params: Spring beans (`*Repository`, `Audit`), `@HttpPathParameter("x") String x`, `@RequestBody Body body`, and `ObjectResponse<T> response` (call `response.send(...)`). Validation failures throw `new HttpException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST | NOT_FOUND)`.

Mutation example — `ProjectsPost.java`:
```java
public class ProjectsPost {
  public void service(@RequestBody NewProject body, ProjectRepository projects,
      ClientRepository clients, ObjectResponse<Project> response) {
    String name = body.getName();
    Long clientId = body.getClientId();
    if (name == null || name.trim().isEmpty() || clientId == null
        || !clients.existsById(clientId)) {
      throw new HttpException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    Project project = new Project();
    project.setName(name.trim());
    project.setClientId(clientId);
    response.send(projects.save(project));
  }
}
```
`InvoicesPost.java`: validates `projectId` exists + `amount != null && amount.signum() > 0`, saves `Invoice`. `ClientsPost.java`: regex-validates email (mirrors frontend + DB CHECK).

Audited mutation example — `InvoicePay.java`:
```java
public class InvoicePay {
  public void service(@HttpPathParameter("id") String id, InvoiceRepository invoices, Audit audit,
      ObjectResponse<Invoice> response) {
    Invoice invoice = invoices.findById(Long.valueOf(id))
        .orElseThrow(() -> new HttpException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND));
    invoice.setStatus("PAID");
    Invoice saved = invoices.save(invoice);
    audit.record("INVOICE_PAID id=" + saved.getId() + " amount="
        + saved.getAmount().setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_UP).toPlainString());
    response.send(saved);
  }
}
```
(A `send` endpoint would mirror this: set status `SENT`, `audit.record("INVOICE_SENT id=" + id + " amount=" + amount...)` — matching the acceptance spec's expected line `INVOICE_SENT id=1 amount=100.00`.)

GET examples: `InvoicesGet` (`@HttpPathParameter("projectId")` → `invoices.findByProjectIdOrderByIdAsc`), `ClientsGet` (`clients.findAllByOrderByIdAsc()`), `ProjectsGet` (`projects.findAllViews()`), `ClientProjectsGet` (`projects.findViewsByClientId(id)`), `DashboardSummaryGet` (counts + `invoices.sumOutstanding()`).

## `Audit` service (`src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/Audit.java`)
`@Service`. Constructor `Audit(@Value("${app.audit.file:.run/audit.log}") String path)`. `synchronized record(String entry)` appends `entry + lineSeparator` with `CREATE, APPEND, SYNC` (creating parent dirs). `synchronized clear()` deletes the file. This is the second assertion channel; use the exact record text the task's test expects.

## `TestSupportController` (`src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/TestSupportController.java`)
`@Profile("harness") @RestController @RequestMapping("/__test__")`, injected `Audit audit, JdbcTemplate jdbc`.
- `POST /reset`: `audit.clear()`, then `SET REFERENTIAL_INTEGRITY FALSE`, `TRUNCATE TABLE invoices/projects/clients RESTART IDENTITY`, `SET REFERENTIAL_INTEGRITY TRUE`.
- `POST /seed` (`@RequestBody Map<String,Object>`): iterates `clients`, `projects`, `invoices` lists, inserting via **explicit-id `jdbc.update` INSERTs** (not JPA save). The invoices insert:
```java
jdbc.update(
  "INSERT INTO invoices (id, project_id, amount, status, issued_date, due_date) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)",
  ((Number) i.get("id")).longValue(),
  ((Number) i.get("projectId")).longValue(),
  ((Number) i.get("amount")).doubleValue(),
  i.getOrDefault("status", "UNPAID"),
  i.get("issuedDate"),
  i.get("dueDate"));
```
**To extend the invoice model** (new column / new status), you extend `reset` (if new tables) and `seed` here so specs can arrange the new fields. This class evolves with the schema (it is not pinned).

## JPA entities & repositories
- `Client` `@Entity @Table("clients")`, id IDENTITY, `name`, `email`. `ClientRepository extends JpaRepository<Client,Long>` with `findAllByOrderByIdAsc()`.
- `Project` `@Entity @Table("projects")`, id, `name`, `@Column("client_id") Long clientId`. `ProjectRepository` has `@Query` constructor-expression methods `findAllViews()` and `findViewsByClientId(@Param clientId)` returning `ProjectView(id,name,clientName)` via join to `Client`. `ProjectView` is a DTO with a 3-arg constructor.
- `Invoice` `@Entity @Table("invoices")`, id, `@Column("project_id") Long projectId`, `BigDecimal amount`, `String status = "UNPAID"`, `@Column("issued_date") String issuedDate`, `@Column("due_date") String dueDate`. `InvoiceRepository` has `findByProjectIdOrderByIdAsc(Long)` and `@Query("SELECT COALESCE(SUM(i.amount),0) FROM Invoice i WHERE i.status='UNPAID') BigDecimal sumOutstanding()`.
- DTO bodies: `NewClient{name,email}`, `NewProject{name,clientId}`, `NewInvoice{projectId,amount:BigDecimal}` — plain getter/setter beans bound via `@RequestBody`.

No standalone `Invoice`-detail DTO/view class beyond the entity (invoices are serialized directly, unlike projects which use `ProjectView` for the client-name join).

## Migrations (`src/main/resources/db/migration/`)
```
V1__clients.sql              clients(id IDENTITY, name NOT NULL, email NOT NULL)
V2__clients_email_format.sql ALTER clients ADD CONSTRAINT clients_email_format CHECK(REGEXP_LIKE(email,'^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$'))
V3__projects.sql             projects(id IDENTITY, name NOT NULL, client_id BIGINT NOT NULL REFERENCES clients(id))
V4__invoices.sql             invoices(id IDENTITY, project_id BIGINT NOT NULL REFERENCES projects(id), amount DECIMAL(12,2) NOT NULL)
V5__invoice_status.sql       ALTER invoices ADD COLUMN status VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'UNPAID'
V6__invoice_dates.sql        ALTER invoices ADD COLUMN issued_date VARCHAR(10); ADD COLUMN due_date VARCHAR(10)
```
All tables use `BIGINT GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY` (so seed can supply explicit ids). New schema = a new `V<n>__*.sql`; never edit an applied one. Dates are stored as ISO `VARCHAR(10)` strings. To change the invoice lifecycle default (e.g. to `DRAFT`), you would add e.g. `V7__invoice_lifecycle.sql` — the existing default is `'UNPAID'`.

---

# 3. Everything referencing "invoice" (case-insensitive)

The invoices feature is already implemented (not merely partial) for the `UNPAID/PAID` model. Files:

Frontend: `features/invoices/{queries.ts, InvoiceForm.tsx, InvoicesTable.tsx, status.slot.tsx, pay.slot.tsx, sort.slot.tsx, due.slot.tsx, issued.slot.tsx}`, `slots/defs/{invoiceRow.ts, invoicesToolbar.ts}`, `routes/projects.$projectId.tsx`, `features/projects/open.slot.tsx` (links to detail where invoices live), `features/dashboard/queries.ts` (outstanding total comment).

Backend: `Invoice.java, InvoiceRepository.java, InvoicesGet.java, InvoicesPost.java, NewInvoice.java, InvoicePay.java, DashboardSummary.java, DashboardSummaryGet.java, TestSupportController.java`; YAMLs `invoices.POST.yml, invoices/{projectId}.GET.yml, invoices/{id}/pay.POST.yml`; migrations `V4/V5/V6`.

**Divergence to be aware of** — `e2e/specs/acceptance.spec.ts` (the current acceptance target) expects an invoice lifecycle the code does **not yet implement**:
- New invoices status `DRAFT`; seed uses `status: 'DRAFT'`.
- A per-row `invoice-send-<id>` button transitioning `DRAFT → SENT`, emitting audit line `INVOICE_SENT id=1 amount=100.00`.
- `invoice-pay-<id>` must be absent (`toHaveCount(0)`) until status is `SENT`, then transitions `SENT → PAID`.

So "adding the invoices feature modeled on projects/clients" most plausibly means implementing this lifecycle by: a new `features/invoices/send.slot.tsx` (model on `pay.slot.tsx`), gating `pay.slot.tsx`'s button on `status==='SENT'` via the slot ctx, a new `invoices/{id}/send.POST.yml` + `InvoiceSend.java` (model on `InvoicePay.java`, audit `INVOICE_SENT`), and a migration changing the status default to `DRAFT`. `TestSupportController.seed` already passes `status` through, so seeding `DRAFT` works without backend edits.

## Seed/audit test helpers (context on the `/__test__` contract)
- `e2e/support/seed.ts`: `resetAndSeed(fixture)` POSTs `/__test__/reset` then `/__test__/seed` (fixture shape `{clients, projects, invoices}` with explicit ids). Throws loudly on non-2xx.
- `e2e/support/audit.ts`: `auditLines()` reads `AUDIT_FILE` (default `../.run/audit.log`), splits non-empty lines — used like `expect(auditLines()).toContain('INVOICE_SENT id=1 amount=100.00')`.

All paths above are under `/home/daniel/ui-sandbox/`. The authoritative rules doc is `/home/daniel/ui-sandbox/CLAUDE.md` (do not edit it, `main.tsx`, `routes/__root.tsx`, `slots/{Slot,registry,discover}.ts`, `api/http.ts`, `query/queryClient.ts`, `vite.config.ts`, `tsconfig.json`, or the `bin/*` scripts).

